PLAN-01  Executive Summary
Objective
Design a secure global Location Switching capability for the POS so changing the active branch updates every location-dependent
module without mixing inventory, sales, cash, permissions, reports, settings, vouchers, price lists, affiliates, or audit history.
Recommendation
Add a visible Current Location entry point in the global header/sidebar, but keep the existing Shift workflow as the only authority for
changing the operating location. Maintain separate operating-location and viewing-location contexts.
Why this fits the existing system
The backend already exposes pos:switch_location and POST /terminal/shifts/:id/switch-location.
TerminalPage already tracks operatingLocationId, viewingLocationId, and queueLocationScopeId.
The Shift UI already validates destination terminals, cash values, current carts, and offline operations.
ADR 0009 and ADR 0031 already require location-scoped inventory, terminal binding, shift-safe transitions, and auditability.
External research
Square uses an explicit in-app Switch location action, location-specific reporting, inventory, devices, and permissions, and warns
against switching with pending offline payments. Toast exposes a location selector while separating location access from
per-location permissions.
Sources: https://squareup.com/help/us/en/article/5580-manage-multiple-locations-with-square ;
https://squareup.com/us/en/point-of-sale/features/multi-store ;
https://support.toasttab.com/en/article/Assigning-Employees-to-Multiple-Locations ;
https://support.toasttab.com/en/article/MLM-Permissions-Guide
Plan status
NOT EXECUTION READY: Phase 354 discovery is still required for voucher, price-list, affiliate, and setting scope, and the
phase ledger must be reconciled with the existing Phase 354-357 location-access documents. The execution skill must
not begin implementation until these gates are closed.
Primary acceptance outcome
An authorized user can move from one authorized operating location to another through an atomic, audited, shift-safe flow, while
read-only users can view authorized location data without gaining transaction or mutation rights.
PLAN-02  Problem and Current State
Problem statement
The POS needs one understandable location context, but operating a branch and merely viewing branch data have different safety
requirements. A free global switch would risk cross-branch sales, stock, cash, queue, and audit errors; a Shift-only entry point is
difficult to discover.
