Current checkout baseline
Branch: feat/DGFY-343-2067-pos-workflow-consolidation.
Baseline commit observed during planning: 786cd4e8329db1a65398ce6aa7eb020ffc8f3b28.
The working tree is dirty with unrelated application, generated, and local skill changes. Implementation must preserve them and
must use a clean, explicitly selected worktree or branch.
Root cause and secondary effects
The root cause is not the absence of location logic. The system already has partial location context and a governed shift transition.
The gap is that the context is not yet presented and reconciled as one cross-module product contract, and not every requested
module has a confirmed scope contract.
Secondary effect: users may interpret viewing a branch as operating that branch.
Secondary effect: adding a global selector without request invalidation could display stale data from the previous branch.
Secondary effect: modules with unclear scope could either leak data or unnecessarily block valid operations.
Documentation constraint
The main implementation phase ledger currently has a high-water mark below the location-access documents, while those
documents define Phase 354 and runtime Phases 355-357. Reconcile the ledger before implementation; do not invent a new
phase sequence.
