Immutable transaction location snapshot.
Later context changes do not rewrite it.
Transition
Atomic shift-location transition record.
Records source, destination, actor, cash, reason, and outcome.
Concept
Authoritative owner
Derived or historical behavior
Audit
Append-only tenant audit trail.
Filter by location for viewing; do not create separate histories.
ADR-001 - Global context with governed operating transition
Decision: use a global header/sidebar entry point that dispatches to the existing Shift-owned operating transition, while preserving a
separate read-only viewing context.
Alternatives rejected: Shift-only switch for poor discoverability; unrestricted sidebar switch for safety risk; duplicate catalogs for data
drift; separate audit stores for incomplete investigation.
Consequences: more explicit context labels and refresh coordination are required, but the design reuses current contracts and is
reversible through a feature flag.
ADR-002 - Shared catalog, location-specific operational state
Decision: keep item identity, SKU, category, and tenant-wide base price centralized; keep stock, availability, visibility, and any
approved overrides location-aware. Add schema only when discovery proves a required location dimension is missing.
