Refresh and race handling
Increment a context version before transition and abort or ignore old requests.
Clear location-dependent caches and carts only according to the approved workflow.
Refresh items, stock, queue, reports, shift, settings, vouchers, pricing, affiliate context, and audit filters after authoritative
success.
Do not refresh a module into a new location until the backend confirms the transition.
Responsive and accessibility requirements
Desktop header selector and mobile sidebar selector expose the same permission-aware flow.
Labels explicitly say Operating Location or Viewing Location.
Focus moves into the transition dialog and returns to the trigger after close.
Warnings are readable without color alone and controls expose disabled reasons.
PLAN-07  Migration and Backward Compatibility
Migration position
No migration is approved yet: First audit existing tables, indexes, constraints, repositories, and queries for vouchers,
price lists, affiliates, settings, reports, and audit. Reuse existing location fields and transition records wherever present.
Required discovery
Map every affected entity to tenant, location, terminal, shift, and historical location fields.
Find all APIs accepting location_id or equivalent filters and classify whether they derive or trust it.
Find all reports and exports that aggregate without an explicit location scope.
Confirm whether settings are stored by tenant, branch, terminal, or mixed scope.
Confirm voucher, price-list, and affiliate ownership and eligibility models.
Safe migration sequence
Stage
Action
Exit evidence
Prepare
Add compatible indexes/columns only when justified; keep old reads/writes working.
Migration tests and schema review pass.
Backfill
Populate location metadata from authoritative terminal, shift, transaction, or grant
sources.
Row counts and ownership parity pass.
Validate
Compare old and new aggregates, reports, and ownership.
No unexplained drift.
Switch reads
Enable location-aware reads behind a feature flag.
Pilot reads match expected data.
Switch writes
Enable location-aware writes and audit.
Integration and reconciliation tests pass.
Observe
Monitor errors, totals, stock, permissions, and audit events.
Observation window passes.
Clean up
Remove compatibility code only after explicit approval.
Rollback window closed.
Backward compatibility
Existing terminals and current shift flows must continue working when the feature flag is off.
Older clients must fail safely or remain on compatible APIs; do not require a new client for an existing safe path without a
migration plan.
Historical reports must remain stable and must not be recomputed from later branch configuration.
Generated build artifacts and unrelated dirty-worktree changes are not migration inputs.
Migration exit criteria
Representative tenant data has been migrated in rehearsal.
Foreign keys, unique constraints, indexes, ownership, null handling, reports, and performance are verified.
Rollback and reconciliation are tested without deleting historical data.
