PLAN-11  Final Recommendation and Execution Handoff
Final recommendation
Build a shared global location context with a visible header/sidebar entry point. Reuse the existing Shift-controlled
operating-location transition. Keep viewing-location navigation read-only and separate from register operation. Extend only the
module contracts proven incomplete by Phase 354 discovery.
What must be built
Global Current Location selector and explicit operating/viewing labels.
Location context coordinator with stale-request protection and module refresh rules.
Server-side location grants, module permissions, terminal binding, shift ownership, idempotency, and audit enforcement.
Location-aware behavior for items, stock, Add Item, sales, parked sales, reports, shifts, settings, vouchers, price lists, affiliates,
queue, and audit.
Verification matrix, migration rehearsal, pilot rollout, observability, and recovery evidence.
What must remain unchanged
The existing Shift switch-location endpoint and governed close/open semantics.
The shared catalog source of truth and location inventory ledger.
Historical transaction location and audit history.
Terminal pairing and strict device safety rules.
Unrelated user changes in the current dirty working tree.
